The value of a module is not the number of classes behind its boundary.  It is
the amount of useful behavior made available through a small interface, minus
the concepts every caller must still understand.

When an interface leaks retries, storage pointers, protocol tokens, and race
handling, the complexity has moved rather than disappeared.
